  {
    "sha": "35b6fed58483a1c688108241065222d9eb3dd8f4",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDM1YjZmZWQ1ODQ4M2ExYzY4ODEwODI0MTA2NTIyMmQ5ZWIzZGQ4ZjQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T10:03:36Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T10:03:36Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): a capped rotary feed is written in the program's unit (#951 review)\n\nIn an inch program the capped F went out as the mm/min number, so the\ncontrol read it as in/min and drove the rotary 25.4x past its stated\nrate. rotaryFeedWord now takes the post's inch flag: mm/min floored to\n0.1, or in/min floored to 0.001 - floored in both, so it never passes the\ncap - with the \"under 0.1 mm/min\" refusal judged once, in mm, before\nconverting. The cap's linear length is judged between the points as\nposted (the post's output step), since an inch word shortens a 0.1 mm\nmove to 0.0039 in and the control times the block over that.\nfanuc.cps and doosan-dnm.cps cap a record carrying any of A, B or C,\nnot A alone.\n\nPinned by rotary_feed_cap: an_inch_program_posts_the_capped_feed_in_inch,\nthe_slow_feed_refusal_is_judged_in_mm_in_both_units,\na_feed_turning_c_alone_holds_the_stated_c_rate.\n\nRefs #885\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
