    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGFlMDMxNTliN2YzYTc3YTgwZWFkYjllMjViY2Y4N2Q0ODdiZjJlYWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-13T10:32:49Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-13T10:32:49Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): cap the rotary feed over the posted length, and judge the posted F word\n\nTwo #951 review findings. The cap measured the move rounded in world\ncoordinates, but the posts write origin-relative ones: with a work\noffset off the output grid (any metric origin, in inch) a one-step move\ncould read as none, the cap took \"tip still\" and F stood over a 0.0001\nin tip move. rotaryFeed now takes the origin and rounds the\norigin-relative coordinates, the words actually written. And an F the\ncap left alone was posted through ff(), which rounds and can land above\nthe cap: rotaryFeed now also judges the rounded word against the limit\nand caps when it would pass it.\n\nPinned by rotary_feed_cap:\na_work_offset_off_the_output_grid_does_not_hide_a_short_move_from_the_cap\nand a_rounded_uncapped_feed_never_posts_above_the_cap (both fail on\nbc5e9b00, fanuc.cps and doosan-dnm.cps, mm and inch).\n\nRefs #885\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
